From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reelee81 <reelee81@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:02:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/18] openjpeg: Decode a requested area exactly like the
 whole image.

opj_tcd_is_subband_area_of_interest() kept a code-block margin of 3
samples for the 9/7 filter, while opj_dwt_decode_partial_97() reads 4,
so a decoded area could differ by 1 from the same area of the whole
image near its edges. The margin is now 4, as tables F.2 and F.3 of the
standard give.

The partial 5/3 transform works on 4 columns at once and computed with
uninitialized memory in the unused columns; its buffer is now cleared.

Modified for ReePDF on 2026-11-11.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 thirdparty/openjpeg/src/lib/openjp2/dwt.c |  4 ++--
 thirdparty/openjpeg/src/lib/openjp2/tcd.c | 14 ++++++--------
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/thirdparty/openjpeg/src/lib/openjp2/dwt.c b/thirdparty/openjpeg/src/lib/openjp2/dwt.c
index d47f0d9..f5d7d32 100644
--- a/thirdparty/openjpeg/src/lib/openjp2/dwt.c
+++ b/thirdparty/openjpeg/src/lib/openjp2/dwt.c
@@ -2924,6 +2924,7 @@ static OPJ_BOOL opj_dwt_decode_partial_tile(
         opj_sparse_array_int32_free(sa);
         return OPJ_FALSE;
     }
+    memset(h.mem, 0, h_mem_size);
 
     v.mem = h.mem;
 
@@ -3870,8 +3871,7 @@ OPJ_BOOL opj_dwt_decode_partial_97(opj_tcd_tilecomp_t* OPJ_RESTRICT tilec,
     opj_v8dwt_t v;
     OPJ_UINT32 resno;
     /* This value matches the maximum left/right extension given in tables */
-    /* F.2 and F.3 of the standard. Note: in opj_tcd_is_subband_area_of_interest() */
-    /* we currently use 3. */
+    /* F.2 and F.3 of the standard, as in opj_tcd_is_subband_area_of_interest(). */
     const OPJ_UINT32 filter_width = 4U;
 
     opj_tcd_resolution_t* tr = tilec->resolutions;
diff --git a/thirdparty/openjpeg/src/lib/openjp2/tcd.c b/thirdparty/openjpeg/src/lib/openjp2/tcd.c
index 96dd16b..03f06a5 100644
--- a/thirdparty/openjpeg/src/lib/openjp2/tcd.c
+++ b/thirdparty/openjpeg/src/lib/openjp2/tcd.c
@@ -2836,15 +2836,13 @@ OPJ_BOOL opj_tcd_is_subband_area_of_interest(opj_tcd_t *tcd,
         OPJ_UINT32 band_x1,
         OPJ_UINT32 band_y1)
 {
-    /* Note: those values for filter_margin are in part the result of */
-    /* experimentation. The value 2 for QMFBID=1 (5x3 filter) can be linked */
-    /* to the maximum left/right extension given in tables F.2 and F.3 of the */
-    /* standard. The value 3 for QMFBID=0 (9x7 filter) is more suspicious, */
-    /* since F.2 and F.3 would lead to 4 instead, so the current 3 might be */
-    /* needed to be bumped to 4, in case inconsistencies are found while */
-    /* decoding parts of irreversible coded images. */
+    /* Note: those values for filter_margin match the maximum left/right */
+    /* extension given in tables F.2 and F.3 of the standard: 2 for QMFBID=1 */
+    /* (5x3 filter) and 4 for QMFBID=0 (9x7 filter). With 3 for the 9x7 */
+    /* filter, a decoded area could differ from the same area of the whole */
+    /* image near its edges. */
     /* See opj_dwt_decode_partial_53 and opj_dwt_decode_partial_97 as well */
-    OPJ_UINT32 filter_margin = (tcd->tcp->tccps[compno].qmfbid == 1) ? 2 : 3;
+    OPJ_UINT32 filter_margin = (tcd->tcp->tccps[compno].qmfbid == 1) ? 2 : 4;
     opj_tcd_tilecomp_t *tilec = &(tcd->tcd_image->tiles->comps[compno]);
     opj_image_comp_t* image_comp = &(tcd->image->comps[compno]);
     /* Compute the intersection of the area of interest, expressed in tile coordinates */
